<article class="env-proposition" id="04QD">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04QD">Proposition <span data-tag="04QD">9.6.8.8</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, let $(S_ L, S_ R)$ be a factorization system on $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let $\operatorname{Fun}_{LR}( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \subseteq \operatorname{Fun}(\Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ be the full subcategory of Notation <a data-tag="04PS" href="/tag/04PS">9.6.7.1</a>. Then the restriction map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  D: \operatorname{Fun}_{LR}( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \quad \quad \sigma \mapsto d^{2}_{1}(\sigma ) \]
</div>
<p> is a trivial Kan fibration. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Condition $(1)$ of Definition <a data-tag="04PD" href="/tag/04PD">9.6.8.1</a> guarantees that $D$ is surjective on objects, and condition $(2)$ guarantees that $D$ is fully faithful (Theorem <a data-tag="04QC" href="/tag/04QC">9.6.7.2</a>). Applying the criterion Theorem <a data-tag="01JX" href="/tag/01JX">4.8.4.1</a>, we deduce that $D$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. Condition $(0)$ of Definition <a data-tag="04PD" href="/tag/04PD">9.6.8.1</a> guarantees that the full subcategory $\operatorname{Fun}_{LR}( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \subseteq \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ is replete, so that $D$ is an isofibration of $\infty $-categories (see Corollary <a data-tag="01F3" href="/tag/01F3">4.4.5.3</a>). Applying Proposition <a data-tag="01G7" href="/tag/01G7">4.5.6.20</a>, we conclude that $D$ is a trivial Kan fibration. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
